What is Laravel in PHP? (Basic Knowledge)
Laravel is a free, open-source PHP framework that helps developers build modern and powerful web applications easily and quickly.
Laravel = A modern PHP toolbox to build secure, fast, and organized web applications.

It makes life easier for developers by giving ready-to-use tools instead of writing everything from scratch.


Key Points:
PHP Framework
Laravel is built using the PHP programming language. It gives you tools and structure to write clean, organized code.

MVC Architecture
Laravel uses the Model-View-Controller (MVC) design pattern.

Model = data (from database)

View = what the user sees (HTML)

Controller = handles the logic between model and view

Routing System
Laravel lets you easily define routes (URLs) and what they should do (like showing a page or saving data).

Blade Template Engine
Laravel has a built-in tool called Blade for writing HTML templates with PHP, in a clean and simple way.

Artisan CLI
Laravel comes with a command-line tool called Artisan that helps you:

Create files (like controllers or models)

Run migrations

Test your app

And more...

Eloquent ORM
Eloquent makes it easy to interact with your database using PHP classes instead of writing raw SQL.

Security & CSRF Protection
Laravel includes built-in security features like:

Form protection

Password hashing

Middleware for access control

Useful Tools

Authentication (login/register)

Validation (check user inputs)

Mail sending

Queue jobs

API support

